			<div class="content" id="post-content-1201368">
									

<p>Hell, it almost feels like it should be on the Anomalous Items log. I mean, it's incredibly easy to maintain, and there's not a whole lot to research on it, and that's pretty much what the LAI list is for.</p>
<p>Here:</p>
<p>Item Description: A 1.5m x 3.6m x 7.6cm pane of reinforced glass that, when viewed by the human eye, shows a partial nighttime view of a city from approximately 400m above ground level.<br />
Date of Recovery: ██-██-████<br />
Location of Recovery: The sixth floor of ████ ██████<br />
Current Status: Hung on the wall of the main reception of Site 33.<br />
Notes: The landscape does not appear to correlate to any location on earth. The city seems to be modern, although it is constructed primarily of Victorian-era architecture. The buildings have often been described as &quot;twisted&quot;, and appear to occupy places they should not.</p>
